# Original feats: fighting styles, epic boons, and general feats for new roles.
# Format: (name, type, prerequisite, text)
FEATS = [
# ---------- fighting styles
("Rider Style", "Fighting Style", "Fighting Style feature",
 "While you are mounted, you gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls with melee weapons, and your mount can use your AC instead of its own if yours is higher."),
("Phalanx Style", "Fighting Style", "Fighting Style feature",
 "While you hold a Shield and you don't have the Incapacitated condition, you and each ally within 5 feet of you gain a +1 bonus to AC. An ally has this bonus only while it is within 5 feet of you, and it gets the bonus from only one creature at a time."),
("Wrestler Style", "Fighting Style", "Fighting Style feature",
 "You can grapple a creature with one hand and attack with a weapon in the other. While you have a creature Grappled, you deal an extra 2 damage when you hit it with a Light weapon or an Unarmed Strike, and the DC to escape your grapple increases by 2."),
("Braced Shot Style", "Fighting Style", "Fighting Style feature",
 "If you haven't moved during your turn, you gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls with Heavy ranged weapons and crossbows until the end of the turn. Moving after the attack doesn't end the bonus for that attack."),
# ---------- epic boons
("Boon of the Wilds", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30. You can't become lost by any means, Beasts and Plants are never hostile to you unless you or your allies harm them first, and you can cast Speak with Animals and Speak with Plants at will without a spell slot."),
("Boon of the Deep Sea", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30. You can breathe water, you have a Swim Speed equal to twice your Speed, and you suffer no harm from cold water or the pressure of the deep. Once per Long Rest, you can cast Control Water without a spell slot."),
("Boon of the Storm", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30. You have Immunity to Lightning and Thunder damage. When a creature within 10 feet of you hits you with a melee attack roll, it takes 2d10 Lightning damage."),
("Boon of Renown", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30. Your name is known across the land. Common folk, guards, and merchants greet you with respect, and you have Advantage on Charisma checks made to deal with them. Once per Long Rest, you can turn a failed Charisma check into a success."),
("Boon of the Bulwark", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30. When an ally you can see within 10 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can take a Reaction to take the damage instead of that ally. Damage you take this way is halved."),
("Boon of the Quarry", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30. When you finish a Long Rest, you can choose one creature that you have seen as your quarry. You always know its direction and distance while it is on the same plane as you, it can't benefit from the Invisible condition against you, and you have Advantage on attack rolls against it. You can have one quarry at a time, and it stays your quarry until you choose another one."),
("Boon of the Lorekeeper", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase your Intelligence or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 30. You can read, speak, and write every language. Once per Long Rest, you can cast Legend Lore without a spell slot or material components."),
("Boon of the Phoenix", "Epic Boon", "Level 19+",
 "Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30. When you are reduced to 0 Hit Points, or when damage would kill you outright, you can burst into flame instead. You regain Hit Points equal to half your Hit Point maximum. This benefit doesn't work against an effect that kills you without reducing you to 0 Hit Points, such as Power Word Kill, or that turns you to dust. Each creature of your choice within 20 feet of you makes a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your Constitution modifier and Proficiency Bonus), taking 6d6 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest."),
# ---------- general feats
("Seafarer", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Strength, Dexterity, or Wisdom. You gain proficiency with Navigator's Tools and Water Vehicles. You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed, and you have Advantage on saving throws to avoid the Prone condition on a ship. A ship whose crew you lead travels 1 mile per hour faster."),
("Beast Bond", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Wisdom or Charisma. A Beast of Challenge Rating 1/4 or lower, such as a Mastiff, a Riding Horse, or a Hawk, becomes your companion. It obeys your spoken commands, acts on your Initiative right after you, and takes the Dodge action unless you take a Bonus Action to command it to take another action. The Beast doesn't grow stronger as you gain levels. If it dies, you can bond with a new Beast when you finish a Long Rest."),
("Siege Engineer", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Intelligence or Constitution. You gain proficiency with Carpenter's Tools and Mason's Tools. Your attacks and spells deal double damage to objects and structures. You can build a simple trap, a barricade, or a ladder in half the normal time, and you know the weak points of walls, gates, and bridges."),
("Monster Slayer", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Strength, Dexterity, or Wisdom. Choose Aberrations, Dragons, Fiends, Giants, Monstrosities, or Undead. You have Advantage on Intelligence checks to recall lore about creatures of that type, and once on each of your turns when you hit one with an attack roll, it takes an extra 1d6 damage of the attack's type. You can change the type when you finish a Long Rest."),
("Escape Artist", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Dexterity. You have Advantage on ability checks and saving throws to avoid or end the Grappled and Restrained conditions. You can move through a space as narrow as 1 foot without squeezing, and you can slip out of nonmagical manacles or ropes in 1 minute."),
("Light Sleeper", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Constitution or Wisdom. You can sleep in Medium or Heavy armor and still gain the full benefits of a Long Rest, you wake at once at any sound louder than a whisper, and you can't be Surprised while you are asleep. You need only 6 hours of sleep to finish a Long Rest."),
("Last Stand", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Constitution. While you have fewer than half your Hit Points, you gain a +1 bonus to AC and to saving throws. When you make a Death Saving Throw, a roll of 18 or 19 also counts as a 20."),
("Spell Echo", "General", "Level 4+, Spellcasting or Pact Magic feature",
 "+1 Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. When you succeed on a saving throw against a spell of level 3 or lower, you can remember its shape. Once before the end of your next turn, you can cast that spell by spending one of your spell slots of the spell's level or higher, using your own spell save DC and spell attack bonus. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest."),
("Bodyguard", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Strength or Constitution. When a creature within 5 feet of you makes an attack roll against an ally of yours, you can take a Reaction to step into the way. The attack targets you instead, and it is made with Disadvantage."),
("Trapsmith", "General", "Level 4+",
 "+1 Dexterity or Intelligence. You gain proficiency with Thieves' Tools or, if you already have it, Expertise with them. You have Advantage on checks to find and disarm traps, and you take half damage from traps. You can set a simple trap that you carry in 1 minute instead of 10."),
]
